qos: 007 draws its 3D view at 1024x608 and stretches it to the 1280x720 front buffer with a filter that reads
whole guest texels, so above render scale 1 the scaled view still reached the screen with 1024 columns (blocky
at 4K; every resolve before it was scaled). After that draw - opaque, reading one resolve destination (bound twice),
no depth, writing an area wider than the source - a linear blit of the host image replaces its result (the area:
scissor, bounded by the viewport). BOTS_GFX_PLAIN_UPSCALE=0 turns it off. The log says "gfx native: plain upscale
done|skipped ..." for the first 8 candidates, with the values that decided it.

diff --git a/src/gfx/vk/draw.cpp b/src/gfx/vk/draw.cpp
index 85619dc..7e4cdd3 100644
--- a/src/gfx/vk/draw.cpp
